<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orange, Vaucluse</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arausio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orange is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the Roman colony of Arausio, founded for veterans around 35 BCE on the land of the Cavares. Its Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and triumphal arch are a World Heritage Site. From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of the Principality of Orange, which passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-nassau">House of Nassau</a> and gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> royal house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orange-vaucluse.jpg" alt="Orange, Vaucluse" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeanlouiszimmermann · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ORANGE-centreville_aerienne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
